sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-collective-06> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Melanocyte conversion after instructor-cell depolarization is a collective, all-or-none decision: different reagents give different incidences in a cohort (e.g. 70% converted), but each animal is either fully converted or fully normal; a computational model fitted to these incidences predicted interventions (two drugs and a dominant-negative construct) that were then confirmed to produce the first partially converted animals.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Melanocyte conversion is all-or-none per animal, stochastic only across the cohort";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "McMillen P, Levin M, “Collective intelligence: A unifying concept for integrating biology across scales and substrates”, Communications biology (2024), doi:10.1038/s42003-024-06037-4; section “Introduction › From normal melanocytes to a melanoma phenotype: a collective decision”. Scope: Xenopus laevis tadpoles with perturbed instructor-cell bioelectric signalling"
}
